We are looking for an experienced FP&amp;A professional to play a central role in our corporate planning, reporting, and cash forecasting processes. This Manager-level role will bring together the consolidated financial outlook and help ensure Finance has a clear, consistent view of company performance across the P&amp;L, balance sheet, and cash flow. 
The role will own key corporate FP&amp;A deliverables, including consolidated forecasting, cash flow modeling and forecasting, Board and ELT reporting, PE sponsor and portfolio company reporting, and GAAP-to-non-GAAP bridges. 
Our approach to FP&amp;A is simple: understand what happened, determine why it matters, and help the business decide what to do next. 
In this role, that means taking inputs from across the FP&amp;A organization and translating them into an accurate, coherent company-level view of performance and outlook. This person will work closely across FP&amp;A, Accounting, Treasury, and the broader Office of the CFO, with significant exposure to senior leadership. 
What You’ll Do 
 Corporate FP&amp;A &amp; consolidation&nbsp;  

Own the consolidation of company forecasts and financial outlooks, bringing together inputs across the FP&amp;A organization into a cohesive company view.&nbsp; 
Maintain an integrated understanding of the P&amp;L, balance sheet, and cash flow and how changes in one area affect the others.&nbsp; 
Analyze company-level performance, risks, opportunities, and changes in outlook. Make recommendations to the business and ELT on ways to improve operational and financial performance.&nbsp; 
Ensure consolidated reporting is accurate, internally consistent, and aligned across FP&amp;A and Accounting.&nbsp; 
Support annual planning, rolling forecasts, long-range planning, and other corporate planning processes.&nbsp; 
Strengthen controls, documentation, and repeatability around core FP&amp;A reporting and consolidation processes.&nbsp; 
Maintain and evolve integrated three-statement models, with particular ownership of balance-sheet forecasting and the linkages between operating performance, working capital, cash flow, and ending cash. 
Contribute to the company’s long-range planning process by translating operating assumptions into multi-year P&amp;L, balance-sheet, cashflow, and free-cash-flow outcomes and helping assess longer-term financial trajectory. 
